    description: "Draw a Bézier curve connecting two points with control points."
    instruction: |
      Draw a Bézier curve from (50, 350) to (350, 50).
      Use bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3, x4, y4).
      Control points: (150, 50) and (250, 350) for a nice S-curve.
    startingCode: |
      function setup() {
        createCanvas(400, 400);
      }

      function draw() {
        background(30);
        stroke(255, 100, 200);
        strokeWeight(3);
        noFill();
        // Draw your bezier curve here
      }
    solution: |
      function setup() {
        createCanvas(400, 400);
      }

      function draw() {
        background(30);
        stroke(255, 100, 200);
        strokeWeight(3);
        noFill();
        bezier(50, 350, 150, 50, 250, 350, 350, 50);
      }
    tasks:
      - id: task-1
        title: "Draw the Bezier"
        instruction: |
          Draw a Bézier curve with bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3, x4, y4).
          Use (50, 350), (150, 50), (250, 350), (350, 50).
        validation:
          - type: functionCall
            name: bezier
            exactArgs: 8
          - type: pixelMatch
            x: 200
            y: 200
            expected: [255, 100, 200]
            tolerance: 120

  - id: exercise-2
    title: "Spline Stroke"
    module: Drawing
    description: "Draw a spline curve through a series of points (p5.js v2)."
    instruction: |
      Draw a smooth spline curve passing through four points.
      Use spline(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3, x4, y4) — the v2 name for what was curve().
      Points: (40, 300), (140, 80), (260, 320), (360, 100).
    startingCode: |
      function setup() {
        createCanvas(400, 400);
      }

      function draw() {
        background(25);
        stroke(100, 200, 255);
        strokeWeight(3);
        noFill();
        // Draw your spline curve here
      }
    solution: |
      function setup() {
        createCanvas(400, 400);
      }

      function draw() {
        background(25);
        stroke(100, 200, 255);
        strokeWeight(3);
        noFill();
        spline(40, 300, 140, 80, 260, 320, 360, 100);
      }
    tasks:
      - id: task-1
        title: "Draw the Spline"
        instruction: |
          Draw a spline with spline(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3, x4, y4).
          Use (40, 300), (140, 80), (260, 320), (360, 100).
          Note: spline() is the p5.js v2 name for the old curve() function.
        validation:
          - type: functionCall
            name: spline
            exactArgs: 8
          - type: pixelMatch
            x: 200
            y: 180
            expected: [100, 200, 255]
            tolerance: 120

  - id: exercise-3
    title: "Curve Points"
    module: Drawing
    description: "Use bezierPoint() to calculate and plot individual points along a Bézier curve."
    instruction: |
      Plot 10 evenly-spaced dots along a Bézier curve.
      Use bezierPoint(x1, x2, x3, x4, t) to get the x and y coordinates at parameter t (0 to 1).
      Draw a small circle at each computed point.
